IOCCC art for the Asciiverse catalog: ASCII Fluid (ascii-fluid) and
Chaos (ioccc-chaos)

These programs are made from two winning entries of the International
Obfuscated C Code Contest (IOCCC, https://www.ioccc.org/):

- 2012/endoh1, "Most complex ASCII fluid" (honorable mention), by
  Yusuke Endoh (https://github.com/mame/), with the author's colour
  version and the scene files that come with the entry (clock.txt by
  HAMANO Tsukasa, the others by the author and the IOCCC judges).
  https://www.ioccc.org/2012/endoh1/index.html
  Copyright (c) 2012-2026 by Landon Curt Noll. Some Rights Reserved.

- 1998/chaos, "Best object orientation", by Alan De Smet
  (http://www.highprogrammer.com/alan/), with its data files.
  https://www.ioccc.org/1998/chaos/index.html
  Copyright (c) 1998-2024 by Landon Curt Noll. Some Rights Reserved.

